"""Present the exact maximum third-order dimension at fourteen qubits."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>'for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed']
 sha=hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest();assert sha in [r.get('certificateSHA256'),r.get('sourceSHA256')]
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)
 css+='\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent subspaces · Exact dimension</p><a href="../../index.html#n=14&t=3">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Fourteen qubits: the maximum third-order dimension is one</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex subspaces</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(14,3)=1.}')+'<p>An exact four-copy positive-definite certificate excludes every two-dimensional third-order AC subspace. A simple three-component Dicke state attains dimension one.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>An explicit state attains the bound</h2>'+m(r'|\psi\rangle=\frac{2|D_{14}^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt{13}|D_{14}^{(7)}\rangle+2|D_{14}^{(14)}\rangle}{\sqrt{21}}.')+'<p>The Dicke support gaps eliminate all off-diagonal tensor components through rank three. The probabilities are '+m(r'(4,13,4)/21',False)+' at magnetic numbers '+m(r'(-7,0,7)',False)+', giving</p>'+m(r'\langle J_z\rangle=\langle J_z^3\rangle=0,\qquad\langle J_z^2\rangle=\frac{56}{3}=\frac{j(j+1)}3,\quad j=7.')+'<p>Thus every normalized vector in its one-dimensional span is third-order AC.</p>'+links([('../../index.html#n=14&t=3&subspace=sparse-third-n14','Coefficients and Majorana representation')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Why a two-dimensional subspace is impossible</h2><div class="proof-step"><h3>1. Encode the full subspace conditions</h3><p>Suppose orthonormal '+m(r'u,v',False)+' span an AC3 plane. Polarization gives '+m(r'PT_{\ell q}P=0',False)+' for every tensor of rank one through three. For '+m(r'w=u\wedge v',False)+', these are exactly the vanishing first-factor contractions of '+m(r'|w\rangle\langle w|',False)+'.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>2. Average four copies over rotations</h3><p>The vector '+m(r'w\otimes w',False)+' lies in the Young subspace '+m(r'\mathbb S_{(2,2)}V_7',False)+': the exterior product is decomposable, so its fully antisymmetric component vanishes. Its rotationally averaged projector '+m(r'X',False)+' is positive and has trace one. The complete Young space has dimension 4200.</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I^{\otimes3})X]=0,\qquad\ell=1,2,3.')+'<p>Real angular-momentum bases reduce the invariant moment to 25 positive multiplicity matrices '+m(r'B_J',False)+' with 1055 real symmetric coordinates in total. Taking real parts preserves all equations, positivity and physical trace, so this covers arbitrary complex subspaces.</p></div>'
 b+='<div class="proof-step"><h3>3. An exact positive functional must vanish</h3><p>The certificate selects 939 necessary equations and supplies rational multipliers. Their exact linear combination is</p>'+m(r'0=\lambda^{\mathsf T}A\mathbf b=\sum_J\operatorname{Tr}(W_JB_J),\qquad W_J\succ0.')+'<p>Every '+m(r'W_J',False)+' is proved positive definite by an exact rational LDL decomposition: all 190 pivots are strictly positive. Since '+m(r'B_J\succeq0',False)+', the equality forces every multiplicity matrix to vanish. Hence '+m(r'X=0',False)+', contradicting trace one.</p><p>The proof requires no numerical rank decision, optimization tolerance, restricted Dicke support or constellation symmetry.</p></div>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact rational certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent physical-word verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Successful exact verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Independent checks and the complete fourteen-qubit row</h2><p>The independent verifier expands physical tensor words, checks the Young symmetry and full angular-momentum decomposition, reconstructs every selected contraction equation, and proves positive definiteness using rational arithmetic. A known exact third-order plane at thirteen qubits is a positive control for the construction. The verifier uses only the Python 3 standard library.</p><pre><code>python3 verify_independently.py</code></pre><p>Combined with the existing first-, second- and fourth-order constructions and the separate fifth-order exclusion, the complete row is now exact:</p>'+m(r'\bigl(K(14,1),\ldots,K(14,7)\bigr)=(5,3,1,1,0,0,0).')+links([('../n14-t5/index.html','No fifth-order state at fourteen qubits'),('../../index.html#n=14&t=3','Updated catalogue')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=14: maximum third-order AC dimension is one</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
